* MiCA Title V\nCrypto-asset service providers
** Ten services (Art. 3(1)(16))
*** Custody and administration (keys)
*** Trading platform
*** Exchange for funds / for crypto-assets
*** Execution, placing, reception and transmission
*** Advice, portfolio management
*** Transfer services
** Entry routes (Arts 59–61)
*** Authorisation as CASP (Art. 63)
*** Notification by banks, investment firms, CSDs, EMIs, fund managers (Art. 60)
*** Registered office, effective management, EU director
*** Reverse solicitation only, lost on any marketing (Art. 61)
** Authorisation (Arts 62–65)
*** Application: 15 items, policies per service
*** 5 + 25 + 40 working days
*** Withdrawal: unused 12 months, dormant 9 months, AML failures
*** Passport: home authority forwards in 10 working days
** Obligations of all CASPs (Arts 66–74)
*** Honest, fair, professional; risk warnings
*** Fees and climate impact published
*** Capital: Class 1 EUR 50 000, Class 2 EUR 125 000, Class 3 EUR 150 000
*** or 1/4 fixed overheads; CET1 or insurance
*** Governance, DORA, records 5 years
*** Client funds to a bank next business day
*** Complaints, conflicts, outsourcing, wind-down plan
** Custody (Art. 75)
*** Agreement, register of positions, custody policy
*** Quarterly statements, return of assets
*** Separate on-chain addresses, insolvency-remote
*** Liability for attributable loss, capped at market value
*** Sub-custody only with authorised CASPs
** Trading platform (Art. 76)
*** Operating rules, suitability of each token
*** No white paper, no admission
*** No anonymised tokens
*** No dealing on own account
*** Pre- and post-trade transparency
*** Settlement on ledger within 24 hours
** Other services (Arts 77–82)
*** Exchange: firm price, execution at displayed price
*** Execution: best result, no routing fees
*** Advice: suitability, independence
*** Transfer: agreement and security
** Acquisitions and size (Arts 83–85)
*** 20 / 30 / 50 % thresholds, 60 working days
*** Significant CASP: 15 million active users
